Carafe: with d3d9.frontEndThread, the Direct3D 9 front end runs on a thread of its own. The game thread keeps a
shadow of render, sampler and texture-stage states and textures, drops a setter that leaves its value as it is, and
appends everything else it can answer at once to a 1 MB ring: states, shaders, streams, constants, transforms,
clears, draws with the data of draws from memory, scenes, state block captures and applies mirrored in the shadow,
DISCARD locks of dynamic buffers staged in memory of its own, and Present, which waits only while the previous frame
is still queued. The worker "dxvk-frontend" replays the ring into the device as it was. Any other call takes the
device lock, which first waits until the worker has emptied the ring; Reset and state block creation run directly.
A multithreaded, D3D8 or D3D9Ex device keeps the plain path. Every 600 frames a [D3D9 front end] line counts calls
queued and dropped, staged locks, drains and waits.
Zlib, as the files it changes.

